  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes. I confess I find it very difficult. I am thirsty almost all of the time, and I try to be disciplined, but it is a real struggle.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:51",
      "end_timestamp": "01:05",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "The long gap over the weekend. By Sunday evening I could drink the tap dry.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:15",
      "end_timestamp": "01:23",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "He keeps a glass by his chair, Doctor, and it ends up empty. Then his ankles blow up by Monday morning.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:24",
      "end_timestamp": "01:36",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Quite so. They are rather swollen on Mondays, and my shoes become a trial.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:47",
      "end_timestamp": "01:56",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Cramps, occasionally. In the calves, towards the last hour. They are quite painful, though they pass.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:10",
      "end_timestamp": "02:20",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Cramps in the last hour of the session, thank you. Let me ask about a few other things. Any chest pain?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:21",
      "end_timestamp": "02:34",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, none.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:35",
      "end_timestamp": "02:37",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any trouble breathing when you lie flat at night?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:40",
      "end_timestamp": "02:45",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, I sleep perfectly well flat, with one pillow.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:46",
      "end_timestamp": "02:52",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And any itching of the skin?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:54",
      "end_timestamp": "02:57",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, not at present.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:58",
      "end_timestamp": "03:01",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Kidney failure for six years now. I was told it came from the high blood pressure, which I have had for twenty years. I also have gout, which flares up now and then.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:10",
      "end_timestamp": "03:30",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I had a fistula put in my arm, four years ago. It works very well.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:38",
      "end_timestamp": "03:46",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Sevelamer, 800 milligrams with meals, for the phosphate. Amlodipine, 5 milligrams once a day. And folic acid, 5 milligrams in the morning.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:55",
      "end_timestamp": "04:07",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "medications[1]",
        "medications[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Lovely, Nadia. So that's sevelamer with meals, amlodipine once a day, and folic acid in the morning. Are you allergic to anything, Mr Chaudhry? Any allergies at all?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:17",
      "end_timestamp": "04:33",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[3]",
        "allergies[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, I have no allergies, Doctor.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:35",
      "end_timestamp": "04:39",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[3]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "Dad, what about that antibiotic last year, in the hospital? You had a bad reaction to it. I don't remember which one it was.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:40",
      "end_timestamp": "04:52",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I do not recall any such thing. I think you may be mistaken, Nadia.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:55",
      "end_timestamp": "05:03",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "Maybe. But the nurse did stop it, I remember that much.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:04",
      "end_timestamp": "05:10",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "There's definite puffiness at the ankles, and it dents when I press with my thumb.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:46",
      "end_timestamp": "05:55",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It's what we'd expect when fluid builds up over the long weekend gap. I can't rule out that your target weight on dialysis needs adjusting too, so we'll keep that in mind. Let me say it back: the thirst drives the drinking, the drinking builds the fluid, and the fluid shows in your ankles and your cramps.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:00",
      "end_timestamp": "06:29",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "A few practical things. Use a small cup, not a glass. Suck on ice chips or a sugar-free sweet when the thirst bites. Go easy on salt, because salt makes you thirstier. And spread your allowance through the day.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:36",
      "end_timestamp": "06:54",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Pickles are salt in disguise, Mr Chaudhry, so perhaps weekends only for now. So: small cup, ice chips, less salt, spread it out.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:05",
      "end_timestamp": "07:19",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "If the swelling isn't better by next week, come and see me again. And do tell the dialysis nurses about the cramps, they can often adjust things during the session.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:25",
      "end_timestamp": "07:42",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]",
        "clinical_actions[2]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
    }
